# Goal 10: Implement __fpclassifyd

## Function
`__fpclassifyd`

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/internal/fpclassifyd.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s2/src/mathd.rs` (line ~786) — exists but not exported via C FFI

## Problem
**Not implemented (FFI gap).** The Rust code has an `fpclassifyd` implementation internally but it is not exported through `lib.rs` as `__fpclassifyd`, so the test binary falls back to the C version. Also verify that the internal implementation uses the correct classification constants (same concern as goal 1 with `__fpclassifyf`).

## What Needs to Change
1. Add a `#[no_mangle] pub extern "C" fn __fpclassifyd(...)` export in `lib.rs` that delegates to the internal Rust implementation.
2. Verify the classification constants match the C version (same enum values as `__fpclassifyf` fix in goal 1).

## Success Criteria
- `__fpclassifyd` is exported via C FFI in `lib.rs`
- Classification results are bitwise-identical to C for all FP classes (NaN, Inf, zero, subnormal, normal)
